{"status":"ok","message-type":"work-list","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"facets":{},"total-results":77655,"items":[{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,8,14]],"date-time":"2026-08-14T12:34:48Z","timestamp":1786710888552,"version":"build-2736575974"},"posted":{"date-parts":[[2022]]},"group-title":"SSRN","reference-count":0,"publisher":"Elsevier BV","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"abstract":"<jats:p>With the growing environmental concerns and the rising number of electric vehicles, researchers and companies are paying more and more attention to green logistics. This paper focuses on the Electric Vehicle Routing problem with time-dependent speeds and soft time windows. The goal is to minimize the total distance traveled and the penalty for arriving early or late at the customers\u2019 locations. We present a Mixed Integer Linear Program (  MILP  ) formulation and propose a General Variable Neighborhood Search (  GVNS  ) metaheuristic as a solution approach. We tested the model and GVNS against the Adaptive Large Neighborhood Search (  ALNS  ) algorithm, using a set of benchmark instances. Experimental evaluation indicates that GVNS can find better quality solutions than MILP and ALNS or the same quality solution in less time.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.2139\/ssrn.4173510","type":"posted-content","created":{"date-parts":[[2022,7,26]],"date-time":"2022-07-26T23:30:15Z","timestamp":1658878215000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["General Variable Neighborhood Search for Electric Vehicle Routing Problem with Time-Dependent Speeds and Soft Time Windows"],"prefix":"10.2139","author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-4575-6720","authenticated-orcid":true,"given":"Luka","family":"Matijevi\u0107","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"78","deposited":{"date-parts":[[2026,8,14]],"date-time":"2026-08-14T11:52:35Z","timestamp":1786708355000},"score":48.1877,"resourc